 "lede": "Sleepyhead started in a basement room of an NYU dorm in 1989: Rachael McNally on drums, Michael Galinsky on bass, Chris O'Rourke on guitar. Their tours fed Half-Cocked, the indie road movie Galinsky co-made.",
 "hero": {
  "src": "https://bigtakeover.com/images/19834.jpg",
  "by": "Photo: via The Big Takeover (2018)"
 },
 "facts": [
  {
   "h": "The first 7-inch, \"Play,\" was produced by Kramer",
   "p": "It came out on Picture Book Artifact in 1991. Albums followed on Slumberland (Punk Rock City USA), Homestead (Starduster, Communist Love Songs) and Sealed Fate (The Brighter Shore).",
   "src": {
    "title": "Sleepyhead (Discogs)",
    "url": "https://www.discogs.com/artist/336852-Sleepyhead"
   }
  },
  {
   "h": "Summer 1990: three dorm-mates move to Providence to become a band",
   "p": "Galinsky writes that they spent it living together, \"trying to figure out how to be a band.\" The first real tour, in summer 1992, was seven or eight shows in two weeks, ending in Chapel Hill.",
   "src": {
    "title": "Half-Cocked: a personal look back (rumur)",
    "url": "https://rumur.com/half-cocked-a-personal-look-back/"
   }
  },
  {
   "h": "Half-Cocked grew out of their tours",
   "p": "Galinsky and Suki Hawley wrote the 1994 film about kids who steal a van full of gear and pretend to be a band. McNally produced it, kept the shoot on schedule and cooked all the meals.",
   "src": {
    "title": "Half-Cocked: a personal look back (rumur)",
